  "properties": {
    "title": "From Japan Forestry Technology Association: miscellaneous notes on nationwide forest open data.",
    "description": "This is an introduction to the nationwide forest open data sets that JAFTA has been involved in developing, such as the National Forest Inventory data, the National Forest Resource Mesh Map Tiles, and the zoning tool \"Morizon\".\n\nJapan Forest Technology Association was established in the summer of 1921 as a vocational organization of the Japanese professional foresters.\r\nThe aim of the association has been to develop and diffuse the technology and science of forestry and to contribute to the cultural advancement of the society through forestry related activities.",
